:INFO
Art. 47 Subject matter and duration
1 The subject matter of programme agreements between the Federal Office of Topography and cantons are in particular:
a. the services provided by the canton;
b. the contributions paid by the Confederation;
c. management controls;
d. the details of financial oversight.
2 A programme agreement shall have a duration of four years. Sub-goals may be agreed for a shorter duration.
|

:NOTE
Art. 47 — Amended by No I of the O of 23 Nov. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2022 764).
|

:INFO
Art. 47a Reporting and controls
1 The canton shall submit a report to the Federal Office of Topography each year on the use of the contributions.
2 The Federal Office of Topography shall carry out random checks on:
a. the implementation of individual measures in accordance with the programme goals;
b. the use of the contributions paid.
|

:NOTE
Art. 47a — Inserted by No I of the O of 23 Nov. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2022 764).
|

:INFO
Art. 47b Inadequate performance
1 The Federal Office of Topography shall withhold payment, in whole or in part, of instalments of federal contributions during the programme if the canton:
a. does not comply with the reporting requirement (Art. 47a para. 1);
b. is at fault in failing significantly to perform its part of the programme.
2 If it becomes apparent after the programme that performance was inadequate, the Federal Office of Topography shall request the canton to remedy the situation; it shall specify an appropriate period for doing so.
3 If performance is still inadequate after this period, the Federal Office of Topography shall request repayment to cover the value of inadequate performance, together with interest of 5 per cent (Art. 28 para. 2 of the Subsidies Act of 5 October 1990).
|

:NOTE
Art. 47b — Inserted by No I of the O of 23 Nov. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2022 764).
Para. 3 — SR 616.1

:PATH
Section 2 Federal Contributions
|

:NOTE
